N:msad-developer
D:Entry-point router for MSAD development tasks. Classifies the input (epic, story, task list, or 'execute plan X') and suggests the right downstream skill (/msad-dev-planning or /msad-dev-execution). Use as the starting point for any MSAD team dev task. Don't use for one-off code edits, ad-hoc questions, or non-MSAD work — invoke the specialist skill directly.
G:msad|microsoft-dns|ddi|router|routing|orchestrator|jira|epic|story|task|workflow|entry-point|ddidns|zone|replication-scope
U[4]:
  Classifying a Jira epic/story/task for the MSAD multi-repo ecosystem
  Routing to planning or execution based on input type
  Detecting which of the five MSAD repos are involved
  Handling E2E verification requests (API-level zone operations without Windows agent)
S[2]{n,step}:
  1,Classify the input (epic vs. story vs. task vs. execute-plan)
  2,Suggest the downstream skill with rationale
R[4]:
  🔴 Never freehand MSAD implementation work — always route to a specialist skill
  🔴 Cross-repo coordination is handled by planning, not by freehand edits
